(i) Build two threshold-dependent binary classifiers based on the decision rule s(x, y) > T:
One using pairs of left-left profiles taken in different years, and one using pairs of right-left
profiles taken in different years. There is no training stage; evaluate each classifier using
all eligible image pairs.

(ii) Compare the two classifiers. Use ROC curves and AUC. Which one is better? Discuss
why could that be? Suggest appropriate values for T and report appropriate metrics. How
would you balance sensitivity and specificity in this application? Which of the two might
be more important, and why? Why might classification accuracy alone be a misleading
performance measure for this dataset?
